# walk_forward_all_candidates.csv is regenerated in full on every run of
# refresh-walk-forward-candidates.yml. The plain .csv is a local/CI working
# file only; keeping it untracked stops it from ever being re-added by
# `git add -u` or `git add -A` by accident.
walk_forward_all_candidates.csv

# walk_forward_all_candidates.csv.gz used to be committed to git on every
# refresh (see refresh-walk-forward-candidates.yml history), but that grew
# the repository by a new ~63MB incompressible blob every week. It is now
# published as a GitHub Release asset instead (release tag
# walk-forward-candidates-latest, uploaded with `gh release upload ...
# --clobber`), and every consumer downloads it from there (falling back to
# a git-tracked copy only during the migration transition, see each
# workflow's "Materialize candidates CSV" step). Keeping it untracked here
# stops it from ever being re-added by `git add -u` or `git add -A` by
# accident.
walk_forward_all_candidates.csv.gz

# train_data.csv is regenerated in full (not appended) on every run of
# daily-model-retrain.yml and refresh-walk-forward-candidates.yml. It is not
# persisted to git at all (not even gzip-compressed): both workflows upload
# it as a 30-day Actions artifact instead, since committing any version of
# it (plain or .gz) grows the repository forever. The plain .csv and any
# leftover .gz are local/CI working files only; keeping them untracked stops
# them from ever being re-added by `git add -u` or `git add -A` by accident.
train_data.csv
train_data.csv.gz
